-- coa19-ch3-powers.l4: Part 25, Chapter 3 (Powers of the Secretary of State): ss 893 and 894, lines 12171-12202 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law as the text states it. The powers to make orders and regulations are machinery (the brief's reason 2) and are listed as inert in NOTES.md;
-- what an order MEANS for a charge, once made, is encoded, with the order's existence and content as plain inputs (never guessed).

§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter 3 Powers of the Secretary of State -- ss 893 and 894`

§§ `s 893 Power to make provision for effect of registration in special register`

-- src:12173 | (1) In this section a “special register” means a register, other than the register, in which a charge to which Chapter A1 applies is required or authorised to be registered.
@ref s 893(1) In this section a "special register" means a register, other than the register, in which a charge to which Chapter A1 applies is required or authorised to be registered (src:12173-12173)
-- "the register" is the registrar's own register (a term defined elsewhere in the Act, outside this part's ranges): the person states whether the register in question is some other register.
GIVEN `the register is a register other than the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a charge to which Chapter A1 applies is required or authorised to be registered in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(1) the register is a special register` MEANS
    IF `the register is a register other than the register` AND `a charge to which Chapter A1 applies is required or authorised to be registered in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “special register” means a register, other than the register, in which a charge to which Chapter A1 applies is required or authorised to be registered"

-- src:12174 | (2) The Secretary of State may by order make provision for facilitating the making of information-sharing arrangements between the person responsible for maintaining a special register (“the responsible person”) and the registrar that meet the requirement in subsection (4).
@ref s 893(2) the person responsible for maintaining a special register ("the responsible person") (src:12174-12174)
GIVEN `the person is responsible for maintaining a special register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(2) the person is the responsible person` MEANS
    IF `the person is responsible for maintaining a special register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person responsible for maintaining a special register (“the responsible person”)"

-- src:12175 | “Information-sharing arrangements” are arrangements to share and make use of information held by the registrar or by the responsible person.
@ref s 893(2) "Information-sharing arrangements" are arrangements to share and make use of information held by the registrar or by the responsible person (src:12175-12175)
GIVEN `the arrangements are arrangements to share and make use of information held by the registrar or by the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(2) the arrangements are information-sharing arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements are arrangements to share and make use of information held by the registrar or by the responsible person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Information-sharing arrangements” are arrangements to share and make use of information held by the registrar or by the responsible person"

-- (3): what an order under this section does to a charge. The Secretary of State's satisfaction and the order's content are inputs.
-- src:12176 | (3) If the Secretary of State is satisfied that appropriate information-sharing arrangements have been made, he may by order provide that—
-- src:12177 | (a) the registrar is authorised not to register a charge of a specified description under Chapter A1,
@ref s 893(3)(a) the registrar is authorised not to register a charge of a specified description under Chapter A1 (src:12176-12177)
GIVEN `an order under section 893 is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is of a description specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(3)(a) the registrar is authorised not to register the charge under Chapter A1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an order under section 893 is in force`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states this effect only of an order made under the section
        IF `the charge is of a description specified in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a charge of a specified description"

-- src:12178 | (b) a charge of a specified description that is registered in the special register within a specified period is to be treated as if it had been registered (and certified by the registrar as registered) in accordance with the requirements of Chapter A1, and
@ref s 893(3)(b) a charge of a specified description that is registered in the special register within a specified period is to be treated as if it had been registered (and certified by the registrar as registered) in accordance with the requirements of Chapter A1 (src:12178-12178)
GIVEN `an order under section 893 is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is of a description specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is registered in the special register within the period specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(3)(b) the charge is to be treated as if it had been registered under Chapter A1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an order under section 893 is in force`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states this effect only of an order made under the section
        IF (NOT `the charge is of a description specified in the order`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a charge of a specified description"
        IF `the charge is registered in the special register within the period specified in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is registered in the special register within a specified period is to be treated as if it had been registered": outside the specified period

-- src:12179 | (c) the other provisions of Chapter A1 apply to a charge so treated with specified modifications.
@ref s 893(3)(c) the other provisions of Chapter A1 apply to a charge so treated with specified modifications (src:12179-12179)
GIVEN `s 893(3)(b) the charge is to be treated as if it had been registered under Chapter A1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(3)(c) the other provisions of Chapter A1 apply to the charge with the modifications the order specifies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 893(3)(b) the charge is to be treated as if it had been registered under Chapter A1`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the other provisions of Chapter A1 apply to a charge so treated with specified modifications": the charge is not so treated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:12180 | (4) The information-sharing arrangements must ensure that persons inspecting the register—
-- src:12181 | (a) are made aware, in a manner appropriate to the inspection, of the existence of charges in the special register which are treated in accordance with provision so made, and
-- src:12182 | (b) are able to obtain information from the special register about any such charge.
@ref s 893(4) The information-sharing arrangements must ensure that persons inspecting the register are made aware of the charges in the special register and are able to obtain information about any such charge (src:12180-12182)
GIVEN `persons inspecting the register are made aware, in a manner appropriate to the inspection, of the existence of charges in the special register which are treated in accordance with provision so made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `persons inspecting the register are able to obtain information from the special register about any such charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(4) the information-sharing arrangements meet the requirement` MEANS
    IF `persons inspecting the register are made aware, in a manner appropriate to the inspection, of the existence of charges in the special register which are treated in accordance with provision so made` AND `persons inspecting the register are able to obtain information from the special register about any such charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information-sharing arrangements must ensure that persons inspecting the register—": a bare "must", not met (fork F-P1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:12190 | (6) In this section “specified” means specified in an order under this section.
@ref s 893(6) In this section "specified" means specified in an order under this section (src:12190-12190)
GIVEN `it is specified in an order under section 893` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 893(6) the description or period is specified` MEANS
    IF `it is specified in an order under section 893`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in an order under this section"
